From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMD TheRock <noreply@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the installed FFTW3Config.cmake relocatable

Upstream's FFTW3Config.cmake.in bakes @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR@ and
@CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR@ -- absolute, build-machine-specific
paths -- into the two legacy FFTW3_LIBRARY_DIRS/FFTW3_INCLUDE_DIRS
variables it sets. Once the staged install is copied to another
machine or build location, those paths no longer exist and consumers
fail with "fftw3.h file not found" (ROCm/TheRock#7781).

This is the only actual defect: upstream's install(EXPORT
FFTW3LibraryDepends ...) -- reached via this file's untouched
include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/FFTW3LibraryDepends.cmake") -- is
already relocatable by construction. CMake auto-generates that export
file with an _IMPORT_PREFIX computed relative to its own install
location, with correct per-configuration paths and Windows
IMPORTED_IMPLIB handling, derived from the real built target. That
mechanism was never broken and needs no changes.

Fixes only the two broken lines, using CMake's own
configure_package_config_file()/PATH_VARS machinery (added to the
configure_file() call in CMakeLists.txt) instead of the raw absolute
substitutions, and leaves everything else in the template -- the
FFTW3LibraryDepends.cmake include, FFTW3_CONFIG_FILE, the legacy
CMake-2.8.3 compatibility shim -- exactly as upstream wrote it.

The CMakeLists.txt hunk uses a wider-than-default context (8 lines
instead of 3) to avoid patch fuzz from a nearby repeated line
("COMPONENT Development)" appears twice close together).

See-also: https://github.com/ROCm/TheRock/issues/7781
---
 CMakeLists.txt       | 6 +++++-
 FFTW3Config.cmake.in | 10 ++++++----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -413,18 +413,22 @@
 set (VERSION ${FFTW_VERSION})
 configure_file (fftw.pc.in fftw3${PREC_SUFFIX}.pc @ONLY)
 install (FILES
           ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/fftw3${PREC_SUFFIX}.pc
          DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/pkgconfig
          COMPONENT Development)
 
 # cmake file
+include (CMakePackageConfigHelpers)
 set (FFTW3_LIBRARIES "FFTW3::${fftw3_lib}")
-configure_file (FFTW3Config.cmake.in FFTW3${PREC_SUFFIX}Config.cmake @ONLY)
+configure_package_config_file (FFTW3Config.cmake.in FFTW3${PREC_SUFFIX}Config.cmake
+  INSTALL_DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/cmake/fftw3${PREC_SUFFIX}
+  PATH_VARS CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR
+)
 configure_file (FFTW3ConfigVersion.cmake.in FFTW3${PREC_SUFFIX}ConfigVersion.cmake @ONLY)
 install (FILES
           ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/FFTW3${PREC_SUFFIX}Config.cmake
           ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/FFTW3${PREC_SUFFIX}ConfigVersion.cmake
 	  DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}/cmake/fftw3${PREC_SUFFIX}
          COMPONENT Development)
 
 export (TARGETS ${fftw3_lib} NAMESPACE FFTW3:: FILE ${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/FFTW3LibraryDepends.cmake)
diff --git a/FFTW3Config.cmake.in b/FFTW3Config.cmake.in
--- a/FFTW3Config.cmake.in
+++ b/FFTW3Config.cmake.in
@@ -3,12 +3,14 @@
   get_filename_component (CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_FILE} PATH)
 endif ()
 
+@PACKAGE_INIT@
+
 # Allows loading FFTW3 settings from another project
 set (FFTW3_CONFIG_FILE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_FILE}")
 
 set (FFTW3@PREC_SUFFIX@_LIBRARIES fftw3@PREC_SUFFIX@)
-set (FFTW3@PREC_SUFFIX@_LIBRARY_DIRS @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR@)
-set (FFTW3@PREC_SUFFIX@_INCLUDE_DIRS @CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR@)
+set (FFTW3@PREC_SUFFIX@_LIBRARY_DIRS "@PACKAGE_CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR@")
+set (FFTW3@PREC_SUFFIX@_INCLUDE_DIRS "@PACKAGE_CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR@")
 
 include ("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/FFTW3LibraryDepends.cmake")
 
--
2.43.0
